_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.1-stable, 4.1-stable\n- Not reproducible in: 4.0-stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using an exported PackedByteArray in the editor, resetting its Size in the Inspector does not free the memory previously allocated.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Attach a new script to any Node.\n2. In the script, write the following code:\n```GDScript\nextends Node\n\n@export var array: PackedByteArray\n```\n3. Select the Node with the attached script in the editor.\n4. In the Inspector, click on the array property.\n5. Set the Size field to 134217728 (128 MiB).\n6. Then, set the Size field back to 0.\n7. Observe that Godot does not free the 128 MiB of memory that was previously allocated.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22054330/issue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"iker-sr","id":220709788,"node_id":"U_kgDODSfDnA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220709788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr","html_url":"https://github.com/iker-sr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iker-sr/received_events","ty